n You check for updates, as with any web request. Network\nfeatures of tools You connect to the local server (for example coding agents)\nare controlled by those tools, not by the Software.\n\n9. SAFETY, HARDWARE AND NO WARRANTY\n\nThe Software streams very large model files from Your SSD and can use most of\nthe memory of Your computer. This reads many gigabytes per request, can increase\nSSD wear, and can slow or interrupt other applications. The Software includes\nmemory and swap protections, but they are estimates and cannot guarantee that\nYour computer will not become slow or unresponsive. Keep Your computer on AC\npower during long sessions and keep backups of important data.\n\nOutput generated by language models can be wrong, unsafe or offensive. You are\nresponsible for checking it before You rely on it.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND \"AS AVAILABLE\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,\nEXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A\nPARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, AVAILABILITY OR ACCURACY. TO THE MAXIMUM\nEXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE LICENSOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL,\nSPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOSS OF DATA, PROFITS OR\nHARDWARE LIFE, ARISING FROM USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE, AND THE\nLICENSOR'S TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM IS LIMITED TO THE AMOUNT YOU PAID FOR THE\nSOFTWARE, WHICH IS ZERO. Some jurisdictions do not allow these limits; in that\ncase they apply only as far as the law permits. Nothing here limits liability\nthat cannot be limited by law (for example for death or personal injury caused by\nnegligence, or for fraud).\n\n10. TERM AND TERMINATION\n\nThis agreement lasts until terminated. It ends automatically if You materially\nbreach it, and You must then stop using and delete the Software. Sections 4, 6, 9\nand 11 survive termination. Termination of this agreement does not affect any\nright You hold under a third-party license.\n\n11. GENERAL\n\nThe Licensor may publish a new version of this agreement with a new release of the\nSoftware; a new version applies to that release and later releases, and does not\nchange the terms of a release You already installed unless You choose to update.\nIf a provision is unenforceable, the rest stays in force. This agreement is the\nwhole agreement about the Software between You and the Licensor. It is governed by\nthe laws of [JURISDICTION], except that mandatory consumer-protection rules of\nYour country of residence continue to apply to You. Contact: [SUPPORT CONTACT /\nGitHub Issues at https://github.com/joyboyreturns/Veystrix/issues].\n\n12. ATTRIBUTION\n\nVeystrix is built on, and includes work derived from, MIT-licensed code that was\npublished as MACQWEN and FlashNext. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the copyright\nholder and the full MIT license text.\n"
